-----------------------------------------------------
The CC BY 4.0 license in Section 1 applies ONLY to original work authored by
Prabal Gupta and consenting Undeciphered.ca contributors. It does NOT override
the copyright, licensing, or repository terms of any third-party material:

  - Holding Archives & Original Manuscripts: Historical ciphertexts, folio
    metadata, and linked scans remain subject to the respective public-domain
    status, copyrights, or repository terms of their holding institutions
    (including Library and Archives Canada, Heritage Canadiana, Archives
    nationales d'outre-mer, Bibliothèque et Archives nationales du Québec,
    Hudson's Bay Company Archives, The Huntington Library, Peel's Prairie
    Provinces, and Internet Archive). No third-party archival document scans
    are hosted in this repository.
  - Government of Canada Publications: Short non-commercial research excerpts
    from Documents on Canadian External Relations (Global Affairs Canada) are
    reproduced under Government of Canada non-commercial reproduction terms
    (https://www.canada.ca/en/transparency/terms.html) and Canadian fair
    dealing. Undeciphered.ca is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
    Government of Canada.
  - University of Ottawa Examination Unit Excerpts: Abbreviated OCR excerpts
    referencing The Canadian Vichy Intercepts (University of Ottawa / Vincent
    Martin-Schreiber) remain licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-
    ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0:
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/) alongside Library and
    Archives Canada RG 24. Any shared adaptation of those University of Ottawa
    excerpts must carry CC BY-SA 4.0 attribution.
  - Background Photographs & Maps: Background photographs and period plates
    are derived from verified Public Domain or CC0 museum collections, and
    map coastlines derive from Natural Earth 1:50m (Public Domain).
  - Website Code: Static HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files in this repository
    are provided strictly AS-IS under the warranty and liability disclaimers
    in Section 2 above. Code contributions and Pull Requests are not accepted.
